<title>INDIA: India 96/97 petro product output seen at 61.5 mlnT.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 petro product output seen at 61.5 mlnT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India hopes to produce 61.5 million tonnes of petroleum products in 1996/97 (April-March) and import around 22.06 million tonnes, junior Petroleum Minister T. R. Balu said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Balu told parliament that the country produced 61.2 million tonnes of petroleum products in calendar 1996 and consumed 75.77 million tonnes in the same period.</p>
<p>He said the demand for petroleum products by the end of the ninth five year plan (1997-2002) was forecast to be 113 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
